eval/gold/export/export-008-compact-process-agreement.json:12:      "content": "For the next export iteration, do not reopen the summary track and do not mix capture-engine fixes into the branch. Keep the work scoped to compact and AI handoff only.",
eval/gold/export/export-008-compact-process-agreement.json:17:      "content": "Understood. We'll treat summary as maintenance-only for now, and keep the branch focused on compact, handoff, and distillation work.",
eval/gold/export/export-008-compact-process-agreement.json:33:      "summary",
eval/gold/export/export-008-compact-process-agreement.json:40:      "summary",
eval/gold/export/export-008-compact-process-agreement.json:50:    "reference": "## Background\n- Title: Collaboration norms for export follow-up work\n- Platform: ChatGPT\n- Context: The thread is establishing working norms for the next export iteration so the branch stays narrow and blocker reporting stays actionable.\n\n## Key Questions\n- How should the next export iteration be scoped?\n- What communication style should be preserved if a blocker appears?\n\n## Decisions And Answers\n- Keep the branch scoped to compact and AI handoff only.\n- Treat summary as maintenance-only for now and do not mix capture-engine fixes into the branch.\n- Report the exact failure mode when blocked instead of giving a broad architecture recap.\n\n## Reusable Artifacts\n- Reference: exact failure mode\n- Reference: narrow export scope\n\n## Unresolved\n- The team may still need to decide when summary leaves maintenance mode.",
eval/gold/export/export-008-compact-process-agreement.json:51:    "experimental_reference": "StartedAt: 2026-03-18T01:00:00Z\nConversation Type: process_agreement\n\n## State Overview\nThis thread is establishing collaboration rules for the next export iteration rather than solving a technical bug directly. The core problem is to keep the branch narrowly scoped to compact and AI handoff work while preserving a reporting style that stays crisp and failure-mode specific. The current state is that summary is frozen to maintenance mode, capture-engine work is out of scope, and the next agent inherits those constraints as working agreement rather than optional preference.\n\n## User Context And Corrections\n- Keep the next export iteration scoped to `compact` and `AI handoff` only.\n- Do not reopen the summary track beyond maintenance work.\n- Do not mix capture-engine, time, or network fixes into the export branch.\n- If a blocker appears, report the exact failure mode instead of responding with a broad architecture recap.\n\n## Open Risks And Next Actions\n- The remaining open process question is when summary should leave maintenance mode without reopening a second front too early."
