eval/gold/export/export-006-summary-important-moves-why.json:2:  "id": "export-006-summary-important-moves-why",
eval/gold/export/export-006-summary-important-moves-why.json:3:  "type": "export",
eval/gold/export/export-006-summary-important-moves-why.json:4:  "mode": "summary",
eval/gold/export/export-006-summary-important-moves-why.json:6:  "title": "Knowledge export framing for future recall",
eval/gold/export/export-006-summary-important-moves-why.json:9:  "messages": [
eval/gold/export/export-006-summary-important-moves-why.json:12:      "content": "For summary mode, do not just preserve chronology mechanically. A future human needs to understand which moves changed the thread and why they mattered.",
eval/gold/export/export-006-summary-important-moves-why.json:32:      "content": "Please preserve the concrete refs too: compactComposer.ts, summaryComposer.ts, and exportCompression.ts, but only when those refs actually help someone reuse the idea later.",
eval/gold/export/export-006-summary-important-moves-why.json:48:      "summaryComposer.ts"
eval/gold/export/export-006-summary-important-moves-why.json:54:    "reference": "## TL;DR\n- The thread tightened Summary so Important Moves explain both what changed and why it mattered, while Reusable Snippets prefer reusable patterns or insights over file references alone.\n\n## Problem Frame\n- Summary should not preserve chronology mechanically.\n- A future reader needs a compact reconstruction of the moves that changed understanding, plus grounded snippets that remain useful without rereading the entire thread.\n\n## Important Moves\n- Move: Reframe `Important Moves` away from raw timeline narration.\n  Why it mattered: This makes the summary useful for future human recall instead of merely mirroring transcript order.\n- Move: Reframe `Reusable Snippets` toward reusable patterns or insights, with file references as supporting anchors when they help.\n  Why it mattered: This turns summary output into a knowledge artifact rather than a list of file paths.\n\n## Reusable Snippets\n- Pattern: Keep `Important Moves` focused on the turns that changed understanding, decisions, or next actions, and explain why each one mattered.\n  Reuse: Useful when turning a long discussion into a future-readable note instead of a timeline dump.\n- Reference: frontend/src/lib/prompts/export/compactComposer.ts\n  Reuse: Useful when comparing how handoff framing differs from knowledge framing.\n- Reference: frontend/src/lib/prompts/export/summaryComposer.ts\n  Reuse: Useful when checking whether Summary keeps future recall as the first priority.\n\n## Next Steps\n- Strengthen the shipped Summary composer so future human recall is the first priority in the system prompt.\n- Re-check whether Kimi follows `Important Moves` and `Reusable Snippets` more reliably once the new exemplar is in place.\n\n## Tags\n- knowledge-export, future-recall, important-moves, reusable-patterns, prompt-composition"
