eval/gold/export/export-001-compact-code-handoff.json:27:      "content": "Plan locked. We'll keep the tray local, route export through exportConversations(...), and preserve the current JSON/TXT/MD rows. The relevant files are frontend/src/sidepanel/components/BatchActionBar.tsx, frontend/src/sidepanel/pages/TimelinePage.tsx, and frontend/src/sidepanel/utils/exportConversations.ts.",
eval/gold/export/export-001-compact-code-handoff.json:32:      "content": "Please preserve concrete artifacts. We still need pnpm -C frontend build, git add -p for mixed files, and a clean commit split for overflow, tray spacing, and export compression.",
eval/gold/export/export-001-compact-code-handoff.json:37:      "content": "Noted. Reusable artifacts include `handleSelectFromMenu`, `suppressNextReaderOpenRef`, `exportMode`, and commands like `pnpm -C frontend build` plus `git add -p frontend/src/sidepanel/components/BatchActionBar.tsx`.",
eval/gold/export/export-001-compact-code-handoff.json:53:    "reference": "## Background\n- Title: Threads batch selection and export tray integration\n- Platform: Claude\n- Context: The thread is hardening Threads Select so overflow actions do not open Reader and batch mode stays local.\n- Constraint: Keep Select All scoped to the current filtered set and reuse Data-style export/delete semantics without bringing back ExportDialog.\n\n## Key Questions\n- How do we stop overflow Select from leaking into OPEN_READER while preserving normal card clicks?\n- How do we keep batch export and delete aligned with the current Threads tray structure?\n\n## Decisions And Answers\n- Add a one-shot suppression guard in ConversationCard.tsx and a second guard in TimelinePage.tsx so overflow Select only enters batch mode.\n- Keep export routed through exportConversations(...) and preserve JSON/TXT/MD rows in the tray instead of restoring ExportDialog.\n- Split the work into focused commits for overflow hardening, tray spacing, and export compression.\n\n## Reusable Artifacts\n- Path: frontend/src/sidepanel/components/BatchActionBar.tsx\n- Path: frontend/src/sidepanel/pages/TimelinePage.tsx\n- API/Function: handleSelectFromMenu(...)\n- API/Function: suppressNextReaderOpenRef\n- Command: pnpm -C frontend build\n- Command: git add -p frontend/src/sidepanel/components/BatchActionBar.tsx\n\n## Unresolved\n- Validate the final tray layout in a narrow viewport after the interaction fixes land.\n- Finish the export compression quality pass before the final commit split.",
eval/gold/export/export-001-compact-code-handoff.json:54:    "experimental_reference": "StartedAt: 2026-03-14T00:00:00Z\nConversation Type: decision + process_agreement\n\n## State Overview\nThis thread is about hardening the Threads selection flow so overflow actions stop leaking into Reader while batch behavior stays local to TimelinePage. The core problem is to isolate the menu-driven selection path, preserve the current tray-based export semantics, and keep the user-facing collaboration constraints explicit instead of rediscovering them later. The current state is that the handoff now needs to carry both the chosen interaction fix and the working agreement that ExportDialog must not return. The next agent inherits a thread where overflow behavior, tray semantics, and clean commit boundaries are already constrained.\n\n## Decisions And Reasoning\n- Overflow Select should enter batch mode without triggering Reader. The chosen path is a one-shot suppression guard in `ConversationCard.tsx` plus a second guard in `TimelinePage.tsx` so the menu action is isolated from normal card activation.\n- Export should continue through `exportConversations(...)` and keep the tray's JSON/TXT/MD rows. Restoring `ExportDialog` was rejected because the user explicitly wanted Data-style batch semantics to stay local to the tray.\n\n## Failed Or Rejected Paths\n- Rejected: bringing back `ExportDialog` as the export surface.\n  Why it was rejected: it would reintroduce a detached flow instead of preserving the current batch tray semantics.\n\n## User Context And Corrections\n- Keep Select All scoped to the current filtered set.\n- Do not reintroduce `ExportDialog`.\n- Preserve concrete artifacts and split commits cleanly for overflow behavior, tray spacing, and export compression.\n\n## Descriptive Anchors\n- `frontend/src/sidepanel/components/BatchActionBar.tsx`\n- `frontend/src/sidepanel/pages/TimelinePage.tsx`\n- `handleSelectFromMenu(...)`\n- `suppressNextReaderOpenRef`\n- `pnpm -C frontend build`\n- `git add -p frontend/src/sidepanel/components/BatchActionBar.tsx`\n\n## Open Risks And Next Actions\n- Validate the final tray layout in a narrow viewport after the interaction fixes land.\n- Confirm the final commit split still matches the overflow/tray/export boundaries."
